course: dictionary
lesson: 8944
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Context tells you which one. «She wore a silk scarf to the party.» You wear a scarf, so silk here means the soft, smooth cloth.
explain: «Spiders spin silk for their webs, and some spider silk is stronger than steel for its weight.» Spiders spin the thread, so silk here means the thread itself. Check by swapping in your meaning: does it still make sense?
explain: The adjective «silky» describes something that feels like silk. «The silky thread» means a smooth, fine thread, not a thread made of silk cloth.
fact: Silk is a soft, smooth, shiny cloth made from threads spun by silkworms.
fact: Silk can also mean the thread itself, made by silkworms or spiders.
fact: «Smooth as silk» means very smooth. «Silky» is the adjective, so a silky scarf feels smooth.
fact: The Silk Road was a long trade route between China and Europe.
fact: In the UK, «silk» can informally mean a senior barrister, and «to take silk» means to become one.
exercise: «Some spider silk is stronger than steel and very stretchy.» What does silk mean here? | A type of bird's nest | A soft, shiny cloth for a scarf | *The thread itself, spun by a spider | A kind of metal
exercise: «Farmers always chose the calmest worms that made the best silk.» What makes the silk in this sentence? | *Silkworms | Bees | Sheep | Spiders in a garden
exercise: «Her new pyjamas felt as smooth as silk.» What does «as smooth as silk» mean? | Very wet and cold | Very loud | Very rough and prickly | *Very smooth
test: What is the Silk Road? | *A long trade route between China and Europe | A river in Madagascar | A type of bridge over a stream | A road made of silk cloth
test: «Caddis fly larvae glue sand grains and tiny shells together with silk into a case.» What is the silk used for? | *To stick things together into a protective case | To float on water | To shine like gold | To make a soft blanket
exam: «A silk scarf is soft and smooth, and silkworms are caterpillars of a moth.» What is a silkworm? | A kind of bird | A small fish | A type of spider | *A caterpillar of a moth
